COMPLETE INSTALLATION + RUN COMMANDS
File Transfer Between Two Virtual Machines Using SCP

STEP 1 — INSTALL OPENSSH IN BOTH VMs
Open terminal in BOTH VMs.
Run:
sudo apt update
Then:
sudo apt install openssh-server -y

STEP 2 — START SSH SERVICE
Run in BOTH VMs:
sudo service ssh start
OR
sudo systemctl start ssh

STEP 3 — CHECK SSH STATUS
sudo systemctl status ssh
You should see:
active (running)
Press:
Q
to exit.

STEP 4 — FIND IP ADDRESS
In VM1:
hostname -I
Example:
192.168.64.5
In VM2:
hostname -I
Example:
192.168.64.6

STEP 5 — TEST NETWORK CONNECTION
From VM1:
ping 192.168.64.6
If working:
Press:
CTRL + C

STEP 6 — CREATE FILE IN VM1
echo "Hello Practical Exam" > demo.txt
Check:
ls

STEP 7 — TRANSFER FILE
scp demo.txt ubuntu@192.168.64.6:/home/ubuntu/
Enter password of VM2.
If asked:
Are you sure you want to continue connecting?
Type:
yes

STEP 8 — VERIFY FILE IN VM2
Go to VM2:
ls
Open file:
cat demo.txt

